From d396cd41f699d25c20f4e5a4b0a7fe14d26fde0a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Michael C. Ferguson" <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 15:18:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/6] usb: dwc2: read HFNUM when comparing against the current
 frame

hsotg->frame_number is a cached copy of HFNUM. It is refreshed at the
top of the common interrupt handler and by the SOF handler, so it is
only reliably current while SOF is unmasked, and only for code running
right after the common handler in the same interrupt.

Two places compare it with the frame the controller is at now but can
run outside those conditions:

- dwc2_schedule_periodic() decides whether next_active_frame of a QH
  with a pending unreserve is already in the past. It is reached from
  dwc2_hcd_urb_enqueue() in process context, where the cached value is
  as old as the last interrupt.
- dwc2_complete_isoc_xfer_ddma() uses it as the frame list index the
  controller is currently at. In descriptor DMA mode, periodic transfers
  do not need SOF, and with threaded interrupts (forced threading or
  PREEMPT_RT) the common handler and the HCD handler run as separate
  threads, so the value can be older than the transfer being completed.

Read HFNUM through dwc2_hcd_get_frame_number() in both places, as
dwc2_pick_first_frame() already does. The value is never older than the
cached one, so in buffer DMA mode this only makes the past-frame check
in dwc2_schedule_periodic() more accurate.

This prepares for not unmasking SOF in descriptor DMA mode, after which
the cached value is no longer refreshed every (micro)frame.

Signed-off-by: Michael C. Ferguson <michael.christopher.ferguson@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c  | 3 ++-
 drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c | 2 +-
 2 files changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c
index 5ec6e79..30ea50b 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_ddma.c
@@ -1029,7 +1029,8 @@ static void dwc2_complete_isoc_xfer_ddma(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg,
 				goto stop_scan;
 
 			qh->td_first = idx;
-			cur_idx = dwc2_frame_list_idx(hsotg->frame_number);
+			cur_idx = dwc2_hcd_get_frame_number(hsotg);
+			cur_idx = dwc2_frame_list_idx(cur_idx);
 			qtd_next = list_first_entry(&qh->qtd_list,
 						    struct dwc2_qtd,
 						    qtd_list_entry);
diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c
index 4f00ff1..b9b253e 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd_queue.c
@@ -1324,7 +1324,7 @@ static int dwc2_schedule_periodic(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg, struct dwc2_qh *qh)
 		 * tightly and we might need to hurry and queue things up.
 		 */
 		if (dwc2_frame_num_le(qh->next_active_frame,
-				      hsotg->frame_number))
+				      dwc2_hcd_get_frame_number(hsotg)))
 			dwc2_pick_first_frame(hsotg, qh);
 	}
 
